From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:31:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: extract H17 camera tuning from current daemon
 locations

Add the IMX958 2224 setfile and the H17 IMX558 1925 setfile to the
legacy extractor, and register 2224 in the native converter. Search both
usr/sbin and usr/libexec for h13/h16 camera daemons and retain their
flattened fallback inputs for device-local firmware updates.

Copy only each setfile's published source length, then zero its alignment
padding. This avoids reading the object after J700's short 1925 file.
Reject conflicting inputs and cover extraction, truncation, padding and
archive interoperability with synthetic data. Document that the existing
raw factory archive preserves iCCl but the ISP upload ABI remains unknown.

Setfile identities and lengths are public driver interoperability facts;
no vendor or per-module calibration bytes are included.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>

